# Cargo's build directory. Hundreds of megabytes after one `cargo check`.
#
# This file ships WITH the seed and becomes the new repository's own
# `.gitignore`, which is where it belongs: `target/` is not ours to know about,
# it is a fact about Rust projects.
#
# It also protects this repository. `pack/2` builds the seed tarball from
# `git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard` — tracked files plus
# untracked ones that are NOT ignored — so a build directory sitting here is
# committed by the next `git add -A` and shipped into every sandbox after that.
# It was: 2,524 files and 466MB, and provisioning failed with
#
#     413 Payload Too Large
#
# from Cloudflare, which reads as an infrastructure limit rather than a seed
# carrying a build cache.
/target

# The database. `DATABASE_PATH` points at `db/app.sqlite3` and WAL makes it
# three files — somebody's local data, never a commit.
/db
